### A token cannot mint a token: minting is something a signed-in person does
# @name BillingMintsAToken
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tokens
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{BillingToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "billing's own",
  "kind": "service",
  "tenantId": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "roles": ["dispatcher"],
  "scopes": ["work_orders:read"],
  "expiresAt": "{{TokenExpiresAt}}"
}

### Dana mints a personal token of her own
# @name DanaMintsPersonal
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "dana's laptop",
  "kind": "personal",
  "tenantId": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "scopes": ["work_orders:read"],
  "expiresAt": "{{TokenExpiresAt}}"
}

### Neither kind of token manages a project: the Management API names the credential and the fix
# @name PersonalAtManagement
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/descriptor
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{DanaMintsPersonal.response.body.$.token}}

###
# @name ServiceAtManagement
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/descriptor
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{BillingToken}}

### No credential at all
# @name AnonymousAtManagement
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/descriptor

### A person's access token: Management does not read `Authorization: Bearer` (spec §5.7), so this is anonymous
# @name BearerAtManagement
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/descriptor
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}

### The control: an operator key the descriptor's `access` admits
# @name AdminAtManagement
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/descriptor
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
